CORE
main.cpp
--cpp11
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] .* relational: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] .* equality: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.3\] .* logical: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.4\] .* not: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.5\] .* decltype: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.6\] .* deduced: SUCCESS$
^\*\* 1 of \d+ failed
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
N5008 [expr.rel]/1, [expr.eq]/1, [expr.log.and]/1, [expr.log.or]/1,
[expr.unary.op]/9: comparisons and the logical operators have type bool, so
sizeof of one is 1; the C front-end's sizeof took them to be int (4).
